title the TAME gate read twelve rooms of nineteen, and both counts of the eighth ban were wrong
prompt Keaton: kg -- the TAME lane, starting with the ban gate that reads five fewer directories than it claims.
think The gate's file set was a find naming twelve directories plus TWO INDIVIDUAL Glow files, so glow/ was governed two sources out of 131 and mycelium, constel, lattice, ember, lantern and scribble were never read at all. The law in .claude/rules/tame-guidance.md states the bans over authored Rye without qualification, and the gate enforcing it covered 684 files where the tree holds 1,108. A roster written as a list grows stale by omission rather than by error: every room added since the list was written was outside the law by default, and nothing compared the two. That is %303's sentence arriving at a second guard within the hour.
think Widening needed a prune before it needed anything else. glow/.cache holds 157 GENERATED .rye plants, machine-written lowering output that no style law governs, so the roster gained ! -path '*/.cache/*' and ! -path '*/bin/*'. Without that the gate would have started failing on code no hand wrote.
think Seven of the eight bans were already clean in the new rooms and gained 424 files of coverage for free. The eighth, ) == error., had eight real violations in constel -- each an assert(call() == error.X) whose silent anyerror upcast is precisely why the ban exists. All eight now read if (call()) |_| unreachable else |err| assert(err == error.X), the form caravan/mapping.rye already used, and fora_apply, fora_read and fora_transfer are GREEN.
think The compound-assert ban looked like a 104-violation wall, and I wrote the honest thing rather than the convenient one: a ban with 104 violations is a ratchet wearing a ban's clothes, so it kept the elder roster with the reason and the door written into both copies. Then the lap walked through that door in the same sitting.
obs BOTH counts of the compound ban were wrong, in opposite directions, and neither error was in the code being judged. The gate's grep 'assert(.* and .*)' cannot tell a conjunction from a quoted string, so six Glow lowering witnesses asserting that generated source CONTAINS text like "pair.p == 5 and pair.q == 3" read as violations and were not. And my own counting regex assert\([^)]* and stopped at the first close paren, so any call standing left of the and hid the conjunction behind it -- four real hits missed in mycelium/braid, lapse, pledge and glow/nock/nock_core_witness.
obs So the row's second lesson is one I earned rather than found: a meter used to SIZE a defect is a claim like any other, and I booked 104 with a regex I had not checked. The true figures are 25 split this lap and 130 remaining in constel alone.
obs tools/fixtures/tame_style_compound_assert.sh blanks quoted content before looking, the way the comment helper blanks comment lines. Six of the seven rooms reached zero and joined the roster; constel alone is held out, and the line to delete when it reaches zero is named in the source rather than left to memory.
obs Every touched module was built and run rather than read: glow_rune_shape, nock_core built directly since it has no rish witness, mycelium_braid, _lapse, _pledge, _freight_conservation, _freight_bron, _freight_true, and the three fora witnesses. mycelium/freight_fixture_gen.rye has no dedicated witness at all, so it was compiled on its own to prove the split held.
loom gate_files_before=684 gate_files_after=1108 rooms_added=7 bans_clean=7 err_eq_fixed=8 compound_split=25 compound_left=130 generated_pruned=157
file tools/t/tame_style_scan_bans.rish the roster widened, and the one ban held back with its door named
file tools/fixtures/tame_style_compound_assert.sh the check that can tell code from a quoted string
file constel/apply.rye eight call-seam error comparisons captured instead
file glow/rune_shape.rye nine mutual-exclusion asserts split so a failure names the pair
file construction/REDS.md %304, carrying the correction of its own first measurement
recommend keep-going -- constel's 130 compound asserts are the next mechanical lap, and the roster line to delete afterwards is written in the source; the four Glow lowering modules with zero asserts and the >70-line ratchet's blindness are the two TAME findings after that
